{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/249653-forsworn-oathbreaker-mechanics","id":249653,"title":"Forsworn/Oathbreaker Mechanics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-05T03:03:04-07:00","id":249653,"title":"Forsworn/Oathbreaker Mechanics","content":"I know when you break a pledge. you suffer the sanction for the length of the Oath Duration from the moment of the break,<br /> <br /> However, being Forswow is a legitimate &quot;title&quot; someone can suffer for a year and a day from the date of the Oathbreak. Usable by anyone who knows about the Oath break.<br /> <br /> The books strongly implies Forsworn are looked down upon, despised, and even under threat of ejection from a Freehold if the Hold is particularly angry.<br /> <br /> I feel that perhaps a social pools penalty should be applicable for any Forsworn. should they try to use a Social pool on a Ling who is aware of the Forsworn's status.<br /> <br /> The question is; IS there a mechanic already in place I have not yet found for those who are Oathbreakers where the Forsworn title is concerned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T20:53:27-07:00","id":253792,"title":"","content":"I don't think this is something that really needs fancified mechanics. A flat penalty to social rolls that involve needing a freehold Lost to trust you would make sense - maybe -2 or -3, depending on your game and the severity of the oath broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"